WEBVTT

00:00.750 --> 00:01.950
This woman...

00:04.160 --> 00:07.470
<i>Maybe it doesn't need to be me who does it.</i>

00:07.470 --> 00:11.530
<i>There may come a day where 
someone else is precious to him.</i>

00:12.150 --> 00:16.490
<i>But... you can't be on your own, Master!</i>

00:17.290 --> 00:20.170
This... doesn't hurt at all.

00:20.660 --> 00:23.620
Not compared to when he told me to leave.

00:24.080 --> 00:26.500
I belong to my master!

00:26.500 --> 00:29.130
I don't want you touching me!

00:29.920 --> 00:31.810
You're just a slave.

00:33.040 --> 00:34.720
Know your place!

00:43.550 --> 00:45.350
Well said, Nephy.

00:48.920 --> 00:51.980
I'd expect nothing less from my apprentice.

00:55.070 --> 00:58.450
Hey, Barbatos. It's been what, a week?

00:58.930 --> 01:00.450
How long have you known?

01:00.750 --> 01:05.370
My suspicions began when that 
Facestealer sorcerer showed up.

01:05.740 --> 01:08.750
I didn't think someone who'd beg for 
their life after encountering me

01:08.750 --> 01:11.460
would be capable of penetrating my barrier.

01:11.760 --> 01:14.210
And only one person came to 
mind when I thought about

01:14.210 --> 01:17.590
who might be making a habit of 
getting through my security.

02:49.020 --> 02:54.020
<b>Episode 6:
If You're An Archdemon, 
You're Practically Obligated To Act Outrageously</b>

02:54.370 --> 02:56.130
Barbatos the Purgatory.

02:54.610 --> 02:57.400
<b>Barbatos the Purgatory</b>

02:56.130 --> 02:57.400
That's what they call you.

02:57.900 --> 03:01.430
Purgatory refers to the realm 
between heaven and the underworld.

03:01.430 --> 03:03.910
Applying that concept to your sorcery, 
you create pocket dimensions,

03:04.200 --> 03:07.600
which helps you specialize in 
transportation and summoning.

03:07.600 --> 03:10.120
You're even better at it than me.

03:10.420 --> 03:13.830
And, just like the Facestealer,
 you showed up after the Angelic Knights

03:13.830 --> 03:17.170
paid me a visit, like you 
were checking on the outcome.

03:17.550 --> 03:20.260
I'd have to be crazy not to 
suspect something after that.

03:21.700 --> 03:26.140
So you knew all along? And you still 
had the nerve to serve me tea.

03:26.410 --> 03:30.000
I was curious about what you were planning.

03:30.000 --> 03:32.560
Now, more importantly...

03:36.160 --> 03:39.860
You've hurt Nephy!

03:44.000 --> 03:45.120
First your arms!

03:47.050 --> 03:48.450
Then your knees!

03:58.160 --> 04:00.760
Sorry... that didn't hurt, did it?

04:01.440 --> 04:04.440
It... did.

04:08.450 --> 04:09.260
But...

04:10.590 --> 04:15.230
You looked a lot more 
hurt than I was, Master.

04:16.170 --> 04:17.150
I did?

04:17.480 --> 04:20.860
I don't know what has 
happened to you, Master.

04:21.320 --> 04:25.740
If you say you don't need me, 
I should probably accept that.

04:25.740 --> 04:26.570
But...

04:28.380 --> 04:32.710
If you have been hurt, 
then I know you're not okay!

04:33.300 --> 04:36.420
Do I seem... hurt to you?

04:36.810 --> 04:37.770
Yes.

04:39.770 --> 04:44.520
Please... don't be alone, Master.

04:44.520 --> 04:45.380
Nephy...

04:47.890 --> 04:50.680
I was the one who left you alone.

04:57.820 --> 05:02.400
Hey, asshole! I'm not dead yet, 
so don't think you've won!

05:02.400 --> 05:03.820
Master!

05:03.820 --> 05:05.070
It's fine.

05:05.680 --> 05:06.950
Nothing's going to happen.

05:15.380 --> 05:19.420
Why? The sorcery is activating, 
but nothing happens!

05:19.730 --> 05:22.560
What... is happening?

05:22.560 --> 05:26.630
Do you remember me describing the 
theoretical ultimate sorcery, before?

05:27.690 --> 05:32.560
Adding circuits to a casting circle from 
the inside, to overwrite the sorcery...

05:32.890 --> 05:36.940
There's actually a little 
trick that makes it possible.

05:39.480 --> 05:44.530
If you use the exact same casting circle, 
you can overwrite it from the inside.

05:45.890 --> 05:47.280
By doing that...

05:47.620 --> 05:50.740
The sorceries will undergo something 
like a harmonic cancellation.

05:51.000 --> 05:55.250
Impossible... is this the 
power of Andras' legacy?!

05:56.290 --> 06:00.080
If he could manage something like 
this, he would've never died.

06:01.640 --> 06:04.510
The first time I used sorcery, 
I was eight years old.

06:05.060 --> 06:08.570
When he captured me, Andras the 
Accursed made a casting circle.

06:09.260 --> 06:12.890
I remembered what it looked like, and 
secretly drew it on the palm of my hand.

06:13.280 --> 06:16.100
With no other tools available, 
I used my own blood.

06:16.410 --> 06:19.620
Looking back now, it was a childish idea.

06:19.620 --> 06:23.520
An amateur shouldn't be able to mimic 
sorcery just by copying its form.

06:24.500 --> 06:28.300
But when I got caught trying to escape, 
and was about to be killed...

06:39.740 --> 06:41.500
It must've been a fluke.

06:41.500 --> 06:48.010
A miracle, only possible because I enacted the
 same sorcery, in only a fraction of a second.

06:48.510 --> 06:51.510
Miracle my ass. You...

06:51.510 --> 06:56.010
What the hell are you?!

07:03.380 --> 07:04.270
This is impossible.

07:04.590 --> 07:07.360
Some of those were sorceries you 
couldn't possibly have seen before!

07:07.910 --> 07:11.610
And you were able to overwrite 
all of them in an instant?!

07:11.950 --> 07:15.530
If that was your best shot, even an amateur 
could manage it, with the right timing.

07:15.530 --> 07:19.290
If you want to call yourself a sorcerer, 
you've got a lot of room for improvement.

07:19.780 --> 07:25.860
Improving sorceries that resonated with me
 instead of simply reacting to them

07:25.860 --> 07:28.710
was my first research project as a sorcerer.

07:29.350 --> 07:34.480
And ever since, I've been cooped up in the 
castle by myself, never talking to anyone,

07:34.480 --> 07:37.220
not even my urchin friends 
from my days on the street.

07:37.700 --> 07:40.900
None of them came looking for me, either.

07:40.900 --> 07:41.730
And yet...

07:44.280 --> 07:46.900
You kept showing up.

07:48.900 --> 07:50.150
<b>Get out!</b>

07:49.110 --> 07:51.800
No matter how obvious I made my annoyance.

07:52.890 --> 07:53.980
Heyo!

07:59.420 --> 08:00.660
Hi...

08:00.660 --> 08:01.660
<b>Slap!</b>

08:04.460 --> 08:07.360
I could have killed you at any time.

08:07.360 --> 08:11.760
I was just curious to see what a 
brat like you was doing in there!

08:12.560 --> 08:13.970
Then let me show you.

08:15.070 --> 08:20.350
Can you tell? I've converted all the casting 
circles you opened up with into this.

08:21.900 --> 08:25.300
Right now it only works as 
physical enhancement sorcery,

08:25.300 --> 08:27.860
but I intend on developing it further.

08:28.210 --> 08:31.820
You... devoured my sorcery?!

08:32.190 --> 08:34.000
Devouring sorcery...

08:34.000 --> 08:36.330
That really is a good way of putting it.

08:36.330 --> 08:39.080
I can see why you were previously 
an Archdemon candidate.

08:40.160 --> 08:43.070
That reminds me, Barbatos the Purgatory...

08:44.330 --> 08:47.920
Now that I'm an Archdemon, 
I have a title of my own.

08:49.030 --> 08:52.090
Let us welcome our new comrade...

08:52.090 --> 08:54.380
And let us grant him his second name.

08:56.010 --> 08:57.660
You will be known as...

08:58.240 --> 09:00.350
The Sorcerer Slayer!

09:00.710 --> 09:03.100
That's what they call me.

09:16.400 --> 09:20.030
<i>He's already eaten all my 
defensive sorceries....</i>

09:20.030 --> 09:24.290
<i>And I've never known anyone who could outdo 
him in terms of physical enhancement!</i>

09:25.190 --> 09:26.140
<i>Which means...</i>

09:27.160 --> 09:32.130
<i>Even if I were an Archdemon, I wouldn't 
be able to stop a punch from him.</i>

09:35.520 --> 09:39.470
Wait... please! You win.

09:42.110 --> 09:45.950
I swear... I'll never show 
my face to you again.

09:46.560 --> 09:50.010
And I'll give you all of 
my knowledge... just...

09:56.650 --> 10:00.200
Zagan... we're friends, right?

10:01.300 --> 10:02.200
Friends?

10:03.360 --> 10:05.700
Can a sorcerer even conceive of that idea?

10:11.510 --> 10:12.590
Chastille!

10:19.450 --> 10:22.800
I'm just playing. No need to panic!

10:23.400 --> 10:25.150
What... do you think you're doing?

10:25.630 --> 10:28.050
I mean, I guess I could kill you,

10:28.050 --> 10:30.820
but that would mean not being 
treated to good liquor anymore.

10:31.300 --> 10:33.510
I don't have a good eye 
for the stuff, myself.

10:33.930 --> 10:36.110
Are you showing me mercy?

10:36.540 --> 10:38.990
I believe this kind of thing 
is called "confidence."

10:39.660 --> 10:40.990
Screw you!

10:41.340 --> 10:45.540
If you let me live, I swear 
I'll kill you! I guarantee it!

10:45.910 --> 10:48.540
Until I see you dead, I'll never give up!

10:48.810 --> 10:53.130
That's fine. As long as drinks 
are on you every time I win.

10:53.600 --> 10:56.860
What are you... even saying?

10:56.860 --> 10:59.800
What could a sorcerer gain 
from not killing an enemy?

11:00.060 --> 11:01.430
That's the thing...

11:01.760 --> 11:06.120
An Archdemon being bound by convention 
is a little ridiculous, isn't it?

11:06.120 --> 11:08.520
I'm going to do whatever I want.

11:08.970 --> 11:11.840
If I want Nephy to live openly in the world,

11:11.840 --> 11:14.770
then I'll just have to seize control of it.

11:16.210 --> 11:18.070
Which is why I won't kill you, either.

11:18.330 --> 11:22.570
If you don't like that, you need to get 
strong enough to force me to change my mind.

11:25.040 --> 11:26.700
You're an arrogant bastard.

11:27.050 --> 11:29.500
What kind of Archdemon 
would I be if I wasn't?

11:41.420 --> 11:44.030
Come on, Barbatos, are you serious?

11:44.030 --> 11:45.680
No... this isn't me.

11:49.020 --> 11:51.180
<i>When I punched the ground,</i>

11:51.550 --> 11:54.610
<i>I must've subconsciously engaged 
with this casting circle!</i>

11:56.570 --> 11:57.520
Nephy, run!

11:58.960 --> 12:00.140
All of you!

12:01.400 --> 12:03.030
What's happening?!

12:09.840 --> 12:12.580
<i>What is this bizarre swell of mana?</i>

12:15.770 --> 12:18.880
Barbatos, what were you trying to do here?!

12:19.280 --> 12:23.340
I was planning on summoning... a true demon.

12:23.840 --> 12:25.330
A demon?!

12:41.990 --> 12:46.990
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

12:47.730 --> 12:48.760
<i>Demons.</i>

12:49.380 --> 12:53.510
<i>They're said to have existed in this world 
in ancient times before leaving it.</i>

12:54.110 --> 12:56.750
<i>There's no proof they ever actually existed,</i>

12:57.320 --> 13:01.340
<i>but there are theories that the symbols used 
in sorcery, as well as those of the Church,</i>

13:01.340 --> 13:06.260
<i>were passed down to 
mortals by gods or devils.</i>

13:06.600 --> 13:10.510
<i>And you were able to summon one of them?!</i>

13:21.590 --> 13:23.860
<i>This is... a "shadow."</i>

13:24.310 --> 13:28.620
<i>No sacrifice and a haphazard activation 
must've resulted in an imperfect summoning.</i>

13:29.040 --> 13:31.370
<i>And in spite of that...</i>

13:36.560 --> 13:37.460
<i>It's over.</i>

13:38.620 --> 13:40.160
<i>We can't win.</i>

13:40.960 --> 13:45.400
<i>Even when I was facing down the Archdemons, 
the pressure wasn't this intense.</i>

13:46.120 --> 13:49.680
<i>This thing... is beyond humankind.</i>

13:50.240 --> 13:52.350
<i>No matter how much power we might gain,</i>

13:52.770 --> 13:56.260
<i>it looks like mortals simply 
can't compare to gods and demons.</i>

14:00.230 --> 14:01.520
<i>Am I going to die?</i>

14:07.630 --> 14:11.870
My king... by your command...

14:15.450 --> 14:18.420
<i>It's... bowing to me?</i>

14:19.090 --> 14:20.230
<i>Wait, no.</i>

14:21.710 --> 14:23.550
<i>The Archdemon emblem?</i>

14:24.170 --> 14:27.010
<i>What exactly have I inherited?</i>

14:27.720 --> 14:29.800
In that case, take your leave!

14:32.320 --> 14:35.720
Begone! This is no place for you.

14:44.050 --> 14:46.520
<i>It's going back... to some other place.</i>

14:46.950 --> 14:49.320
<i>Wherever they all dwell, most likely.</i>

15:05.220 --> 15:07.340
Not good! The cave is collapsing!

15:08.660 --> 15:09.170
Nephy!

15:09.170 --> 15:10.420
Master!

15:12.670 --> 15:14.330
Hang on, Miss Chastille!

15:14.330 --> 15:15.820
Get onto my back!

15:18.180 --> 15:19.730
You too, come on!

15:28.240 --> 15:29.690
Lady Chastille!

15:29.960 --> 15:32.260
Lady Chastille!

15:35.440 --> 15:38.690
Lady Chastille! I'm so 
relieved you're all right!

15:40.000 --> 15:44.170
Listen well! Our priority is ensuring 
Lady Chastille and the citizens are safe!

15:44.480 --> 15:49.200
It's not like we're aiding and
 abetting some wicked sorcerer!

15:49.200 --> 15:50.800
Fine. Just go.

15:51.170 --> 15:52.980
You're just brushing us off?!

15:52.980 --> 15:54.920
Torres, let's just go.

15:54.920 --> 15:57.700
The guy's got a serious attitude problem.

15:57.700 --> 16:00.480
Mister Sorcerer, thank you for saving us!

16:01.090 --> 16:03.920
You two need to work this out, okay?

16:06.270 --> 16:08.480
See you around, Nephy!

16:10.540 --> 16:11.780
So...

16:11.780 --> 16:14.240
Do you want to keep fighting, Barbatos?

16:16.000 --> 16:18.970
After what I just saw? 
What the hell could I do?

16:24.710 --> 16:26.670
So... what now?

16:27.320 --> 16:30.510
I bring you some good booze, 
and you let me off the hook?

16:30.830 --> 16:33.630
Yeah. Make sure it's quality stuff.

16:36.540 --> 16:37.510
Yeah, okay.

16:47.560 --> 16:49.820
<b>Gasp!</b>

16:48.510 --> 16:49.820
<i>We're alone!</i>

16:50.170 --> 16:52.970
<i>What do I do? What should I say to her...</i>

16:52.970 --> 16:54.220
Master.

16:55.280 --> 16:58.280
I would like to remain at your side.

16:59.750 --> 17:02.290
Are you sure? You don't have to...

17:04.300 --> 17:06.210
I want to be with you, Master.

17:07.920 --> 17:11.020
Well... you've become stronger, haven't you?

17:11.760 --> 17:14.190
But some things will have to change.

17:18.000 --> 17:20.290
<i>There's something I need to tell her.</i>

17:20.710 --> 17:25.130
<i>I hurt you, Nephy, but I won't 
ever leave you alone again.</i>

17:25.130 --> 17:27.990
<i>I swear to protect you. So...</i>

17:29.880 --> 17:33.280
I want you to call me by 
my name, not "Master."

17:33.740 --> 17:36.450
Not a slave, or my servant, or my apprentice.

17:36.450 --> 17:38.280
I want something else for us!

17:39.510 --> 17:41.450
Y-You mean...

17:41.990 --> 17:44.450
I'm saying... I...

17:46.550 --> 17:47.190
l...

17:48.340 --> 17:49.230
lo...

17:50.330 --> 17:51.590
Ugh!

17:52.130 --> 17:54.290
You belong to me!

17:54.290 --> 17:57.740
And you always will! Forever! 
Until one of us dies!

17:57.740 --> 17:59.180
No, even after that!

18:07.940 --> 18:11.400
<i>Why can't I say something 
as simple as "I love you"?!</i>

18:14.050 --> 18:15.070
Yes!

18:15.490 --> 18:17.900
<i>Nephy... smiled.</i>

18:21.200 --> 18:24.240
Could you please put this back on me?

18:25.240 --> 18:28.500
No, that's a bad idea. It's a slave collar.

18:28.850 --> 18:32.290
But I want it. Considering 
it's how Master and I...

18:33.260 --> 18:37.260
How Lord Zagan and 
I first became connected.

18:37.760 --> 18:39.010
Very well.

18:42.090 --> 18:45.560
<i>It's a bit imposing for an
 engagement ring, but,</i>

18:46.050 --> 18:48.940
<i>I suppose this still makes us...</i>

18:58.070 --> 18:59.870
Um, Lord Zagan?

19:01.200 --> 19:06.200
What exactly is our relationship if I'm not 
your slave, servant, or apprentice anymore?

19:08.440 --> 19:11.120
<i>I wish I knew!</i>

19:12.720 --> 19:16.090
<i>Could someone please tell me?</i>

19:20.140 --> 19:23.700
<i>I'm an Archdemon with a dilemma...</i>

19:23.700 --> 19:25.500
<i>How do I love my elf bride?</i>

19:31.420 --> 19:34.150
Hey, did you hear? There's a new Archdemon!

19:34.150 --> 19:37.230
Yeah, the sorcerer that lives 
in the Lost Woods, right?

19:37.230 --> 19:38.570
With the scary face.

19:38.570 --> 19:41.020
But he's supposed to be a decent sort.

19:41.020 --> 19:44.700
Yeah, I heard he saved 
someone from some brigands.

19:45.060 --> 19:48.280
Everyone's talking about the new Archdemon.

19:49.100 --> 19:52.040
A toast to the newly crowned 
young Archdemon, then.

19:52.370 --> 19:54.430
It doesn't bother you?

19:54.430 --> 19:57.800
I had thought you were certain to be
 the next Archdemon, Gremory.

19:58.200 --> 19:59.380
Hardly.

20:00.800 --> 20:03.980
Try not to get too drunk so early in the day.

20:03.980 --> 20:06.240
Just you watch, Kimaris.

20:06.240 --> 20:08.680
Things are going to change around here.

20:09.100 --> 20:14.150
If he's replacing Marchosias, does that 
mean he's the new lord of Kianoides?

20:14.150 --> 20:18.600
I've seen him come to town to shop in person, 
even though he's an Archdemon.

20:18.600 --> 20:21.840
And he's always got a beautiful elf with him.

20:21.840 --> 20:22.650
Oh, right!

20:22.970 --> 20:25.420
Is that his girlfriend? Or maybe his wife?

20:26.000 --> 20:26.870
Oh, sorry!

20:30.270 --> 20:31.250
Watch it, idiot!

20:35.540 --> 20:38.000
And you won't reconsider?

20:38.000 --> 20:38.750
No, sir.

20:39.050 --> 20:44.340
You refuse to lead the hunt for 
the 13th Archdemon, Zagan?

20:44.760 --> 20:47.560
<i>He's saved my life twice.</i>

20:47.560 --> 20:49.670
<i>I cannot betray that.</i>

20:49.670 --> 20:51.010
Cardinal Clavwell.

20:51.010 --> 20:55.440
As I've testified, he was not involved 
in the string of kidnappings.

20:55.440 --> 20:56.980
He is innocent.

20:57.330 --> 20:59.450
You'd defend a sorcerer?

20:59.450 --> 21:01.280
Such words carry grave weight.

21:03.380 --> 21:04.850
I am aware.

21:04.850 --> 21:06.990
I see. In that case...

21:07.480 --> 21:09.700
Chastille Lillqvist.

21:10.410 --> 21:14.960
You are hereby relieved of your position 
as an Angelic Knight indefinitely.

21:15.420 --> 21:19.290
<i>They care more about censuring their 
own than dealing with the Archdemons.</i>

21:19.770 --> 21:23.800
<i>It seems the Church has hit a new low.</i>

21:24.120 --> 21:27.780
Please, Cardinal Clavwell! 
This punishment is too much!

21:27.780 --> 21:31.680
We ask that you consider 
Lady Chastille's past accomplishments!

21:31.940 --> 21:36.340
And the loss of one of the
 Sacred Swords during the ascent

21:36.340 --> 21:39.380
of a new Archdemon will only sow chaos!

21:39.380 --> 21:40.900
Enough, you three!

21:45.280 --> 21:48.950
<i>That man never once strayed 
from what he believed in.</i>

21:54.550 --> 21:58.000
<i>I want to be able to do the same!</i>

23:29.970 --> 23:34.970
<b>Next Time:
 Even An Archdemon Should Know
 Better Than To Hit A Child</b>
